# THE REMAINING 167. Every rust_test below already existed with a `needs-postgres` label and
# executed in no workflow step. A rust_test target alone is not wiring; this sh_test is, and the
# indirection is also the credential control — test_needs_postgres.sh refuses a raw //backend/...
# target because that bypasses the loader.
#
# Wired in one tranche because the marginal cost was MEASURED, not estimated: 11 wrappers 996s,
# 19 wrappers 1032s, i.e. ~4.5s each. The dependency build (2773 commands, 0% cache) dominates and
# is paid once. An earlier claim in this repository that the cost is "roughly linear" and that this
# many "is not viable" was wrong, and is retracted in the program ledger.

